ific microbial signatures (Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium).\n\n**P0192** (2022, fulltext): Comprehensive review on gut microbiota influence on immunotherapy.\n- Relevant to CH03 (mechanisms) and CH04 (interventions - FMT, probiotics).\n- Specific value: Detailed mechanism pathways (A2AR, HDAC, STING), clinical intervention data.\n\n**P0193** (2025, fulltext): Veillonella/Streptococcus aging and ICI efficacy in solid tumors.\n- Relevant to CH02 (microbial features - age-stratified) and CH03 (mechanisms - CD8+ T cell infiltration).\n- Specific value: Age-specific microbial markers, small sample limitation noted.\n\n**P0194** (2026, fulltext): Microbiome-driven diagnostic/therapeutic strategies review.\n- Relevant to CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (interventions).\n- Specific value: Lists specific species, mechanisms (SCFA, barrier function), intervention strategies.\n\n**P0195** (2023, fulltext): DAT metabolite enhances T-cell priming and ICI.\n- Relevant to CH03 (mechanisms - IFN-I signaling) and CH04 (metabolite supplementation).\n- Specific value: Specific metabolite (DAT) mechanism validation in mouse models, antibiotic recovery context.\n\n**P0196** (2025, fulltext): Immunometabolism and microbiota crosstalk review.\n- Relevant to CH03 (mechanisms - metabolic pathways) and CH05 (limitations - TME metabolic competition).\n- Specific value: Integrates immunometabolism perspective, explains why beneficial microbiome may not always work.\n\n**P0197** (2025, abstract_only): FMT-LUMINate trial abstract, NSCLC and melanoma.\n- Relevant to CH01 (clinical evidence - FMT trials) and CH04 (interventions - FMT safety/efficacy).\n- Specific value: ORR data (80% NSCLC, 75% melanoma), toxicity differences by ICI regimen.\n\n**P0198** (2024, abstract_only): Fasting mediated microbiome modulation in RCC.\n- Relevant to CH03 (mechanisms - tryptophan metabolites) and CH04 (dietary interventions).\n- Specific value: Diet-microbiome-ICI causal chain via FMT, trypto